---
layout: docs.njk
title: Docs
description: The gemifi docs, collected from the repo when the site is built - the device YAML, every component, the platforms and chips, and which devices have been tested on hardware.
permalink: /docs/
# Its cards repeat every page's summary: the search would find this page for everything.
searchable: false
crumb: gemifi
lede: Everything a device YAML can hold, one page per component as in ESPHome, and the chips and devices it runs on. Each page is a README in the repo, collected when the site is built.
---
<section class="section tone tone-overview">
  <h2 id="start">Start here</h2>
  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li><article class="card"><h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ '/get-started/' | url }}">Get started</a></h3><p>Run the dashboard, write a YAML, build and flash.</p></article></li>
    {% for c in docs.core %}
    <li><article class="card"><h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ c.url | url }}">{{ c.title }}</a></h3><p>{% if loop.first %}The whole YAML format: pins, the device keys, presets, DAW feedback and the generated code.{% else %}What each component costs in time, RAM and flash on each platform.{% endif %}</p></article></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

{% for g in [docs.base].concat(docs.groups) %}
<section class="section tone tone-{{ g.key }}">
  <h2 id="{{ g.key }}">{{ g.title }}</h2>
  {% if g.intro %}<p class="section-intro">{{ g.intro }}</p>{% endif %}
  <ul class="card-grid">
    {% for i in g.items %}
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ i.url | url }}"><code>{{ i.title }}</code></a></h3>
        <p>{{ i.summary }}</p>
        {% if i.of %}
        <div class="card-foot">
          <span class="docs-base-of tone tone-{{ i.of.key }}">base of {% if i.of.shown %}<a href="#{{ i.of.key }}">{{ i.of.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ i.of.title }}{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{% endfor %}

<section class="section tone tone-platforms">
  <h2 id="platforms">Platforms</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">The chip families gemifi builds for. A device YAML picks one with <code>platform:</code>. <a href="{{ '/docs/platforms/' | url }}">All platforms</a> has them side by side.</p>
  <ul class="card-grid">
    {% for p in docs.platforms %}
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ p.url | url }}">{{ p.title }}</a></h3>
        <div class="card-foot"><span class="status status-{{ p.status }}">{{ statuses[p.status].label }}</span></div>
      </article>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section tone tone-devices">
  <h2 id="devices">Devices</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    <a href="{{ '/docs/devices/' | url }}">Tested devices</a> lists every device YAML in the repo and what has been checked on hardware.
  </p>
  <ul class="card-grid">
    {% for d in collections.devices %}
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ d.url | url }}">{{ d.data.maker }} {{ d.data.model }}</a></h3>
        <div class="card-foot"><span class="status status-{{ d.data.status }}">{{ statuses[d.data.status].label }}</span></div>
      </article>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

{% for g in docs.guides %}
<section class="section tone tone-{{ g.key }}">
  <h2 id="{{ g.key }}">{{ g.title }}</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">{{ g.intro }}</p>
  <ul class="card-grid">
    {% for i in g.items %}
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ i.url | url }}">{{ i.title }}</a></h3>
        <p>{{ i.summary }}</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{% endfor %}
